// Wave 1 acceptance: most basic single-target damage ability.
// Lowers to AbilityProgram { gate: { cooldown_ticks: 10, range: 5.0 },
//                            effects: [EffectOp::Damage { amount: 30.0 }],
//                            per_effect_areas: [Some(EffectAreaShape{
//                                kind: Circle, args: [0.5, 0, 0, 0] })] }
//
// Damage tuning rationale (2026-05-04 #85 retune): bumped from 15 to
// 30 so combat resolves by tick ~150 even with shield_hp absorption
// active (50-shield ShieldUp cycles absorb ~1.6 strikes per cooldown
// at this damage; net dmg per 120-tick cycle ≈ 60 hp; combat
// converges in ~140 ticks).
//
// `in circle(0.5)` exercises Wave 1.5#2 in-shape lowering — declares
// the AOE intent at the .ability surface (lands in
// program.per_effect_areas as ShapeKind::Circle, args[0] = 0.5). The
// 0.5 radius is small enough to be effectively single-target in the
// duel_abilities 2-agent fixture (no second enemy can be inside the
// disc), so the .sim's existing single-target verb is correct
// behavior. Real AOE spatial dispatch (verb iterating multiple
// candidates via spatial.within / for_each_neighbor) lands in a
// multi-agent fixture later — this E2E pins the lowering metadata.

ability Strike {
    target: enemy
    range: 5.0
    cooldown: 1s
    hint: damage

    damage 30 in circle(0.5) [PHYSICAL: 100]
}
